Request rate is flat at about 25 req/s across the window, so load doesn't explain the spikes. Median latency holds around 0.35s, and the tail is what moves. The pool config is as Run #4 described: one connection per process, no overflow, and a 5s wait. Eight gthread threads per worker share that connection, so requests can queue behind it. That is a real constraint, but it does not line up with the onset. I did not confirm the running build or read the API logs, so no root cause is established.

